# Family Studio for Rhino: local settings
#
# Copy this file to rhino/.env. Every value is optional. The build copies .env next to the
# plug-in (FamilyStudio.rhp); you can also keep one at %APPDATA%\FamilyStudio\.env.
# Never commit .env.
#
# The Rhino plug-in is a hello-world panel for now. It reads these values only to show, in its
# title block, what is configured. The same keys drive the Revit plug-in.

# =============================================================================================
# OpenAI: ChatGPT sign-in through Codex
# =============================================================================================
# There is no key to paste. Sign in with ChatGPT from the Family Studio window in Revit (or run
# "codex login" with CODEX_HOME set to this folder). Rhino and Revit share the same default folder:
#     %LOCALAPPDATA%\FamilyStudio\codex-home
# To reuse the Codex app's own sign-in instead:
#     OPENAI_CODEX_HOME=%USERPROFILE%\.codex
OPENAI_CODEX_HOME=
OPENAI_CODEX_PATH=
OPENAI_CODEX_MODEL=
OPENAI_CODEX_REASONING_EFFORT=
